<title>JAPAN: Nippon Dantai Life reveals problem loans.</title>
<headline>Nippon Dantai Life reveals problem loans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Dantai Life Insurance Co has disclosed its restructured loans (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Sep 96     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans		5.8	     41.6</p>
<p>  Bad loans			  45.0		9.4</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	    5.4		6.3</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	    56.2	     57.3</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more.</p>
</text>
